            <title>[LU-20082] LNet: TCP receive buffer size setting not taking effect.</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20082</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;When using the &lt;b&gt;lnet_sock_setbuf&lt;/b&gt; function to set &lt;b&gt;txbufsize&lt;/b&gt; and &lt;b&gt;rxbufsize&lt;/b&gt;, there is an issue: &lt;b&gt;rxbufsize&lt;/b&gt; is incorrectly assigned to &lt;b&gt;sk-&amp;gt;sk_sndbuf&lt;/b&gt;. This causes both &lt;b&gt;sk_sndbuf&lt;/b&gt; and &lt;b&gt;sk_rcvbuf&lt;/b&gt; to behave unexpectedly.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This issue was introduced during the refactoring to support kernel 5.8 due to kernel interface changes. Refer to &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-13783" title="Support for linux kernel version 5.8" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-13783"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-13783&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Code:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="code panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="codeContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre class="code-java"&gt;
void
lnet_sock_setbuf(struct socket *sock, &lt;span class="code-object"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; txbufsize, &lt;span class="code-object"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; rxbufsize)
{
        struct sock *sk = sock-&amp;gt;sk;

        &lt;span class="code-keyword"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; (txbufsize != 0) {
                sk-&amp;gt;sk_userlocks |= SOCK_SNDBUF_LOCK;
                sk-&amp;gt;sk_sndbuf = txbufsize;
                sk-&amp;gt;sk_write_space(sk);
        }

        &lt;span class="code-keyword"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; (rxbufsize != 0) {
                sk-&amp;gt;sk_userlocks |= SOCK_RCVBUF_LOCK;
                sk-&amp;gt;sk_sndbuf = rxbufsize;
        }
}&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;`&lt;b&gt;sk-&amp;gt;sk_sndbuf = rxbufsize&lt;/b&gt;` should be `&lt;b&gt;sk-&amp;gt;sk_rcvbuf = rxbufsize&lt;/b&gt;`.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;</description>
